        "answer": {
          "short": "$0.\\dot{6}$. The calculator rounds the infinitely recurring decimal to fit its finite display.",
          "worked": "$\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}&=0.666666\\ldots\\\\&=0.\\dot{6}\\end{aligned}$\n\nThe digit $6$ repeats forever. A calculator has a finite display, so a rounded display ending in $7$ is an approximation rather than the exact value.",
